    {
      "@id": "item/name-key",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 7,
      "name": "One name-comparison rule all three drivers agree on",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/50",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:4-data-model"
      ],
      "size": "S",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [],
      "doneWhen": "Support\\NameKey is unit-tested directly; File and Directory maintain name_key in a saving hook and expose whereNamed(), which replaces every where('name', ...) collision check; the migration applies utf8mb4_bin only on mysql and mariadb; three tests -- a differently-cased upload adds a version, an accented name creates a second file, and an NFD name matches its NFC twin -- are each shown failing on at least one driver before the fix and green on all six legs after; the stored name is unchanged when an upload versions an existing file.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-17T08:13:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-17T08:39:26Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/53"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/content-actions",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 8,
      "name": "Rename and move actions for directories and files",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/9",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:4-data-model"
      ],
      "size": "S",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [
        "item/name-key"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "Each action has a test that a caller lacking edit or manage is refused, through a Policy rather than in the action; a rename or move into a name a live sibling already holds throws the existing Duplicate exceptions under the NameKey rule, asserted on all three matrix legs; the pre-existing MoveDirectory, TrashFile and RestoreFile gain the same refusal coverage.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-17T08:45:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-17T10:42:13Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/55"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/trash-directory",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 9,
      "name": "Trashing a directory hides everything beneath it",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/49",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:4-data-model"
      ],
      "size": "M",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [
        "item/name-key"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "A file in a live descendant of a trashed directory is absent from Services\\Search results and from the browser for a viewer granted on an ancestor, asserted against the query rather than the rendered view; that test fails on main with no code change and is mutation-checked; TrashDirectory cascades through Eloquent so each projection is forgotten; RestoreDirectory reverses it and leaves independently trashed files trashed; both require manage, refused through a Policy.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-17T10:40:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-17T11:18:20Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/63"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/schema-query-audit",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 10,
      "name": "Audit every semantic inherited from a driver default instead of stated",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/60",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:4-data-model"
      ],
      "size": "M",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [],
      "doneWhen": "A SchemaPortabilityTest runs on all six legs: it computes each index key width against utf8mb4 worst case and asserts it fits InnoDB 3072 and PostgreSQL 2704 or is an explicitly listed driver-conditional expression; it round-trips a maximum-length 4-byte-character value through every indexed varchar, shown failing on pgsql for properties.value_string first; every foreign key column has an index leading with that column; a checked-in inventory names every raw-SQL or collation-dependent site and the test fails when one is not registered; every column compared against user input for equality or uniqueness is listed with its folding rule.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-17T11:24:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-17T11:53:08Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/66"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/pgsql-value-string-index",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 11,
      "name": "Give PostgreSQL an index strategy for value_string",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/39",
